{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  pf-search  —  PrintFabrix search overlay (trigger + dialog)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rendered TWICE from Pfheader.liquid, with different parts:

      {% render 'pf-search', part: 'trigger', display_style: '…' %}
      {% render 'pf-search', part: 'overlay', quick_menu: …, trending: … %}

  The trigger may appear more than once (the header renders a desktop
  copy and a drawer copy). The overlay must be rendered EXACTLY ONCE
  per page — it carries the CSS and the JS.

  WHY A <dialog> AND WHY IT MOVES TO <body>
    The header is position:sticky, has `contain: layout style`, and on
    some templates sits inside a transformed ancestor. Any position:fixed
    child of that subtree gets clipped to the header. showModal() puts
    the element in the top layer, which escapes all of it — and on init
    the dialog is re-parented to <body> so even a non-modal fallback
    (or a browser mid-upgrade) can never be trapped inside the header.

  RECOMMENDATIONS (the panel you see before typing)
    Rendered server-side, so opening the overlay costs zero requests:
      · Recent searches   — localStorage, newest first, max 6
      · Popular searches  — `quick_menu` linklist, as chips
      · Trending products — first N products of `trending` collection
    Recent searches are injected client-side into the slot that is
    already in the DOM, so there is no layout jump.

  LIVE RESULTS
    routes.predictive_search_url (/search/suggest.json) — products,
    collections, pages, articles and query completions. Debounced,
    de-duplicated, in-memory cached, and every in-flight request is
    aborted when the next keystroke lands.

    Prices are deliberately NOT shown: suggest.json returns a bare
    price string whose unit (cents vs. major) is not guaranteed across
    markets, and a wrong price on a made-to-order product is worse than
    no price. Product type is shown instead.

  VOICE SEARCH
    Web Speech API (SpeechRecognition / webkitSpeechRecognition).
    Chrome, Edge and Safari 14.1+ support it; the mic button stays
    hidden everywhere else, so nothing dead is ever on screen.
    Interim words stream into the input as they are spoken; the final
    transcript runs the search. It does NOT auto-navigate — the results
    are shown and the visitor picks. Permission denial, no microphone
    and silence all get their own message.

  ACCESSIBILITY
    Input is a combobox driving a listbox; ↑/↓ move aria-activedescendant,
    Enter opens the active row, Escape closes (mic first, then dialog).
    Status line is aria-live="polite". <dialog> handles the focus trap
    and returns focus to the trigger on close.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pfs_part = part | default: 'trigger'
  assign pfs_placeholder = placeholder | default: 'Search fabrics, sizes, finishes…'
  assign pfs_label = label | default: 'Search'
-%}

{%- if pfs_part == 'trigger' -%}
  {%- comment -%} ─────────── TRIGGER ─────────── {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `search-action` keeps the header grid placing this exactly where the stock
    trigger sat; `header-actions__action` opts it into the theme's sibling-dim
    hover and icon sizing; `button-unstyled` strips the theme's button chrome.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button
    type="button"
    class="search-action pf-search-trigger header-actions__action button-unstyled{% if display_style == 'text' %} search-action--text header-actions__text-style{% endif %}{% if class != blank %} {{ class | strip }}{% endif %}"
    data-pf-search-open
    aria-haspopup="dialog"
    aria-controls="pf-search-overlay"
    aria-label="{{ pfs_label | escape }}"
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      Same swap as the stock trigger: in text mode the word shows on desktop
      and the icon takes over on mobile, where there is only a 44px cell.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span
      class="svg-wrapper pf-search-trigger__icon{% if display_style == 'text' %} desktop:hidden{% endif %}"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" focusable="false">
        <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="6.25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <path d="M13.6 13.6 17.5 17.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
    {%- if display_style == 'text' -%}
      <span class="pf-search-trigger__label mobile:hidden">{{ pfs_label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </button>

{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%} ─────────── OVERLAY ─────────── {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign pfs_trending_limit = trending_limit | default: 4

    # The chips shown before anyone types, in order of preference. Whichever
    # wins, the row is never empty — an empty panel on a first visit is worse
    # than a generic one, and "recent searches" is empty for everybody the
    # first time.
    #   1. terms the merchant typed into the "Suggested searches" setting
    #   2. the pinned list below
    #   3. their popular-searches menu
    #
    # WHY THE LIST IS PINNED HERE
    # The Browse row used to be collections and nothing else, and Shopify
    # hands those over alphabetically — so the panel opened on "All Fabrics,
    # Blockout & Backlit, Building Wraps, Café Barriers…", which is an
    # accident of the alphabet rather than what PrintFabrix wants people to
    # search for. These lead the row now; the collections follow underneath.
    #
    # Editable without touching this file: anything typed into the header's
    # "Suggested searches" setting replaces this list wholesale.
    assign pfs_pinned = 'Scaffolding, Fence Banner, Stage Banners, Event Backdrops, Curtains and Drapes, Printed Double Sided Fabric, Custom Printed Stretch Fabric, Mesh Polyester Fabric, Backlit Polyester Lightbox'
    assign pfs_terms = suggestions | default: pfs_pinned | split: ','

    assign pfs_has_quick = false
    if quick_menu != blank and quick_menu.links.size > 0
      assign pfs_has_quick = true
    endif

    assign pfs_has_trending = false
    if trending != blank and trending.products.size > 0
      assign pfs_has_trending = true
    endif
  -%}

  <dialog id="pf-search-overlay" class="pf-search" aria-label="{{ pfs_label | escape }}">
    <script type="application/json" data-pf-search-config>
      {
        "suggestUrl": {{ routes.predictive_search_url | default: '/search/suggest' | json }},
        "searchUrl": {{ routes.search_url | default: '/search' | json }},
        "lang": {{ request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en' | json }},
        "voice": {% if voice == false %}false{% else %}true{% endif %},
        "limit": 5
      }
    </script>

    <div class="pf-search__sheet">
      {%- comment -%}
        A real GET form to /search, so Enter, the Search button and a
        JS-off visitor all land on the native results page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <form
        class="pf-search__bar"
        action="{{ routes.search_url }}"
        method="get"
        role="search"
        data-pf-search-form
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">

        <span class="pf-search__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" focusable="false">
            <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="6.25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/>
            <path d="M13.6 13.6 17.5 17.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </span>

        <input
          class="pf-search__input"
          type="search"
          name="q"
          id="pf-search-input"
          placeholder="{{ pfs_placeholder | escape }}"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocorrect="off"
          autocapitalize="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          enterkeyhint="search"
          role="combobox"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="pf-search-results"
          aria-autocomplete="list"
          aria-describedby="pf-search-status"
          data-pf-search-input
        >

        <button type="button" class="pf-search__clear" data-pf-search-clear aria-label="Clear search" hidden>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M6 6l8 8M14 6l-8 8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <button
          type="button"
          class="pf-search__mic"
          data-pf-search-mic
          aria-pressed="false"
          aria-label="Search by voice"
          title="Search by voice"
          hidden
        >
          <span class="pf-search__mic-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <rect x="7.4" y="2.2" width="5.2" height="9.4" rx="2.6" fill="currentColor"/>
            <path d="M4.4 9.2a5.6 5.6 0 0 0 11.2 0" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M10 14.8v3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <button type="submit" class="pf-search__go">{{ pfs_label }}</button>

        <button type="button" class="pf-search__close" data-pf-search-close aria-label="Close search">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M5 5l10 10M15 5L5 15" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </form>

      <p class="pf-search__status" id="pf-search-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

      <div class="pf-search__body" data-pf-search-body>
        {%- comment -%} Live results land here. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div id="pf-search-results" class="pf-search__results" role="listbox" aria-label="Search results" hidden></div>

        {%- comment -%} …and this is what shows before anyone types. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="pf-search__default" data-pf-search-default>
          <section class="pf-search__group" data-pf-recent-group hidden>
            <div class="pf-search__group-head">
              <h2 class="pf-search__group-title">Recent searches</h2>
              <button type="button" class="pf-search__group-action" data-pf-recent-clear>Clear</button>
            </div>
            <div class="pf-search__chips" data-pf-recent-list></div>
          </section>

          {%- comment -%}
            Term chips carry a real /search href so they work with JS off and
            read as links to crawlers; the script intercepts the click and runs
            the search inside the panel instead of navigating away.

            ONE row, two sources: the pinned terms first, the store's own
            collections after them. These used to be exclusive branches of the
            same if — terms OR collections, never both — so filling in the
            suggestions setting did not push the collections down the row, it
            deleted them from the panel.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if pfs_terms.size > 0 or collections.size > 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A lookup of what is already pinned, so the same thing is not
              offered twice. Delimited with pipes because a bare `contains` is
              a substring test: "Canvas" would otherwise be swallowed by
              "Canvas & Natural". " and " folds to " & " on both sides, which
              is what lets the pinned "Curtains and Drapes" recognise the
              "Curtains & Drapes" collection as the same row.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- capture pfs_pinned_keys %}{% for term in pfs_terms %}|{{ term | strip | downcase | replace: '&amp;', '&' | replace: ' and ', ' & ' }}{% endfor %}|{% endcapture -%}
            <section class="pf-search__group">
              <div class="pf-search__group-head">
                <h2 class="pf-search__group-title">Browse</h2>
                {%- if collections.size > 0 -%}
                  <a class="pf-search__group-action" href="{{ routes.collections_url }}">All collections</a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="pf-search__chips">
                {%- for term in pfs_terms limit: 12 -%}
                  {%- assign pfs_term = term | strip -%}
                  {%- if pfs_term != blank -%}
                    <a
                      class="pf-search__chip"
                      href="{{ routes.search_url }}?q={{ pfs_term | url_encode }}&amp;options%5Bprefix%5D=last"
                      data-pf-suggest-term="{{ pfs_term | escape }}"
                    >
                      <span class="pf-search__chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span>{{ pfs_term }}</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- for pfs_collection in collections limit: 8 -%}
                  {%- capture pfs_coll_key %}|{{ pfs_collection.title | strip | downcase | replace: '&amp;', '&' | replace: ' and ', ' & ' }}|{% endcapture -%}
                  {%- unless pfs_collection.handle == 'all' or pfs_pinned_keys contains pfs_coll_key -%}
                    <a class="pf-search__chip" href="{{ pfs_collection.url }}">
                      <span class="pf-search__chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                      <span>{{ pfs_collection.title }}</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- endunless -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </section>
          {%- comment -%}
            Only reachable if the pinned list above is emptied AND the store
            has no collections — the popular-searches menu is the fallback for
            a panel that would otherwise open bare.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- elsif pfs_has_quick -%}
            <section class="pf-search__group">
              <div class="pf-search__group-head">
                <h2 class="pf-search__group-title">Popular right now</h2>
              </div>
              <div class="pf-search__chips">
                {%- for link in quick_menu.links limit: 10 -%}
                  <a class="pf-search__chip" href="{{ link.url }}">
                    <span class="pf-search__chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span>{{ link.title }}</span>
                  </a>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </section>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if pfs_has_trending -%}
            <section class="pf-search__group">
              <div class="pf-search__group-head">
                <h2 class="pf-search__group-title">{{ trending.title | default: 'Trending' }}</h2>
                <a class="pf-search__group-action" href="{{ trending.url }}">View all</a>
              </div>
              <div class="pf-search__tiles">
                {%- for product in trending.products limit: pfs_trending_limit -%}
                  <a class="pf-search__tile" href="{{ product.url }}">
                    <span class="pf-search__tile-media">
                      {%- if product.featured_media -%}
                        {{
                          product.featured_media
                          | image_url: width: 240
                          | image_tag:
                            loading: 'lazy',
                            width: 120,
                            height: 120,
                            sizes: '120px',
                            alt: product.featured_media.alt
                        }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="pf-search__tile-title">{{ product.title }}</span>
                  </a>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </section>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  {%- comment -%} ─────────── STYLES ─────────── {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    /* Brand tokens, local to the overlay so nothing leaks into the theme. */
    .pf-search {
      --pfs-magenta: #e20a6e;
      --pfs-magenta-dk: #c1085d;
      --pfs-navy: #141c33;
      --pfs-ink: #10182c;
      --pfs-cyan: #0899b4;
      --pfs-body: #5a6580;
      --pfs-line: #e4e8f2;
      --pfs-line-2: #eef1f7;
      --pfs-surface: #fff;
      --pfs-surface-2: #f7f9fd;
      --pfs-radius: 18px;
      --pfs-shadow: 0 32px 70px -24px rgb(16 24 44 / 38%), 0 4px 14px rgb(16 24 44 / 8%);
      --pfs-speed: 180ms;
      --pfs-ease: cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.9, 0.3, 1);

      width: min(760px, calc(100vw - 32px));
      max-width: none;
      max-height: min(78vh, 720px);
      padding: 0;
      margin: 9vh auto auto;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: var(--pfs-radius);
      background: var(--pfs-surface);
      box-shadow: var(--pfs-shadow);
      color: var(--pfs-ink);
      overflow: visible;
      /* The theme sets its own font on dialogs in places; pin ours. */
      font-family: inherit;
    }

    .pf-search::backdrop {
      background: rgb(10 16 30 / 55%);
      backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    }

    .pf-search[open] {
      display: flex;
      animation: pf-search-in var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search[open]::backdrop {
      animation: pf-search-fade var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    @keyframes pf-search-in {
      from {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(-10px) scale(0.99);
      }
    }

    @keyframes pf-search-fade {
      from {
        opacity: 0;
      }
    }

    .pf-search__sheet {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      width: 100%;
      min-height: 0;
      max-height: inherit;
      border-radius: inherit;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    /* ── Search bar ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pf-search__bar {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      flex: none;
      padding: 14px 14px 14px 18px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pfs-line);
      background: var(--pfs-surface);
    }

    .pf-search__bar-icon {
      display: flex;
      flex: none;
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
      color: var(--pfs-body);
      transition: color var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search__bar-icon svg {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
    }

    .pf-search__bar:focus-within .pf-search__bar-icon {
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
    }

    .pf-search__input {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
      height: 34px;
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
      outline: none;
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--pfs-ink);
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: 17px;
      font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      appearance: none;
    }

    .pf-search__input::placeholder {
      color: #97a1b8;
      font-weight: 400;
    }

    /* Kill the UA clear button — we ship our own. */
    .pf-search__input::-webkit-search-cancel-button,
    .pf-search__input::-webkit-search-decoration {
      appearance: none;
      display: none;
    }

    .pf-search__clear,
    .pf-search__mic,
    .pf-search__close {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      flex: none;
      width: 36px;
      height: 36px;
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--pfs-body);
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: background var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease), color var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search__clear svg,
    .pf-search__close svg {
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
    }

    .pf-search__mic svg {
      width: 19px;
      height: 19px;
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
    }

    .pf-search__clear:hover,
    .pf-search__close:hover,
    .pf-search__mic:hover {
      background: var(--pfs-surface-2);
      color: var(--pfs-ink);
    }

    /* The theme resets outline:none globally — force the ring back. */
    .pf-search :is(button, a, input):focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--pfs-magenta) !important;
      outline-offset: 2px !important;
      border-radius: 10px;
    }

    .pf-search__mic {
      position: relative;
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
    }

    .pf-search__mic-pulse {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--pfs-magenta);
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(0.6);
    }

    .pf-search__mic[aria-pressed='true'] {
      background: var(--pfs-magenta);
      color: #fff;
    }

    .pf-search__mic[aria-pressed='true'] .pf-search__mic-pulse {
      animation: pf-search-pulse 1.4s var(--pfs-ease) infinite;
    }

    @keyframes pf-search-pulse {
      0% {
        opacity: 0.45;
        transform: scale(0.7);
      }

      100% {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: scale(1.9);
      }
    }

    .pf-search__go {
      flex: none;
      height: 40px;
      padding: 0 20px;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--pfs-magenta);
      color: #fff;
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: background var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search__go:hover {
      background: var(--pfs-magenta-dk);
    }

    .pf-search__close {
      margin-inline-start: 2px;
    }

    /* ── Status line ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pf-search__status {
      flex: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0 18px;
      max-height: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 34px;
      color: var(--pfs-body);
      transition: max-height var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search__status:not(:empty) {
      max-height: 34px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pfs-line-2);
    }

    .pf-search__status[data-tone='error'] {
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .pf-search__status[data-tone='listening'] {
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    /* ── Scrolling body ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pf-search__body {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-height: 0;
      overflow-y: auto;
      overscroll-behavior: contain;
      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
      scrollbar-width: thin;
    }

    .pf-search__group {
      padding: 16px 18px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pfs-line-2);
    }

    .pf-search__group:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .pf-search__group-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .pf-search__group-title {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #8a94ad;
    }

    .pf-search__group-action {
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
      background: none;
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .pf-search__group-action:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    /* ── Chips (recent + popular) ───────────────────────────────── */
    .pf-search__chips {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .pf-search__chip {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 7px;
      max-width: 100%;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--pfs-line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--pfs-surface);
      color: var(--pfs-ink);
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: 13.5px;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.2;
      text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: border-color var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease), background var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease),
        color var(--pfs-speed) var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search__chip span:not(.pf-search__chip-dot) {
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .pf-search__chip:hover {
      border-color: var(--pfs-magenta);
      background: #fdecf2;
      color: var(--pfs-magenta-dk);
    }

    .pf-search__chip-dot {
      width: 6px;
      height: 6px;
      flex: none;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--pfs-cyan);
    }

    .pf-search__chip--recent .pf-search__chip-dot {
      background: #c3cadb;
    }

    /* ── Trending tiles ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pf-search__tiles {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .pf-search__tile {
      display: block;
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .pf-search__tile-media {
      display: block;
      aspect-ratio: 1;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      border: 1px solid var(--pfs-line-2);
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--pfs-surface-2);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .pf-search__tile-media img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      transition: transform 320ms var(--pfs-ease);
    }

    .pf-search__tile:hover .pf-search__tile-media img {
      transform: scale(1.05);
    }

    .pf-search__tile-title {
      display: -webkit-box;
      -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
      -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
      overflow: hidden;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    /* ── Live results ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pf-search__row {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 9px 10px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer;
      scroll-margin: 12px;
    }

    .pf-search__row:hover,
    .pf-search__row[data-active='true'] {
      background: var(--pfs-surface-2);
    }

    .pf-search__row[data-active='true'] {
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--pfs-line);
    }

    .pf-search__row-media {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      flex: none;
      width: 46px;
      height: 46px;
      border: 1px solid var(--pfs-line-2);
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: var(--pfs-surface-2);
      overflow: hidden;
      color: #9aa4bb;
    }

    .pf-search__row-media img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
    }

    .pf-search__row-media svg {
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
    }

    .pf-search__row-text {
      min-width: 0;
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }

    .pf-search__row-title {
      display: block;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      white-space: nowrap;
      font-size: 14.5px;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .pf-search__row-title mark {
      background: none;
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .pf-search__row-meta {
      display: block;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      white-space: nowrap;
      font-size: 12.5px;
      color: var(--pfs-body);
    }

    .pf-search__row-arrow {
      flex: none;
      color: #c3cadb;
      font-size: 15px;
    }

    .pf-search__all {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--pfs-line-2);
      background: var(--pfs-surface-2);
      color: var(--pfs-ink);
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .pf-search__all:hover,
    .pf-search__all[data-active='true'] {
      color: var(--pfs-magenta);
    }

    .pf-search__empty {
      padding: 34px 18px 40px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .pf-search__empty-title {
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .pf-search__empty-body {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--pfs-body);
    }

